config FMT
	bool "fmt: text formatting into caller memory"
	default y
	select STATUS
	help
	  Integers in decimal and hex, strings, and hex dumps, written into
	  a buffer the caller provides, plus a printf-style front end.
	  No floating point. Freestanding: needs only memcpy().

choice FMT_DIGITS
	prompt "fmt: number conversion"
	default FMT_BUILTIN
	depends on FMT
	help
	  What turns a number into digits. Output, statuses, and truncation
	  are identical either way, and nothing a caller sees changes.

config FMT_BUILTIN
	bool "Built-in conversion"
	help
	  Shifts and adds, so it needs no division helper and no C library
	  beyond memcpy(). The right choice unless the image already links
	  the C library's printf.

config FMT_LIBC
	bool "The C library's snprintf()"
	depends on PLATFORM_SNPRINTF
	help
	  Each number is converted by snprintf() into a scratch buffer and
	  copied only if it fits whole. For an image that links printf
	  anyway (for logging, say), where the built-in conversion would be a
	  second copy of the same code. Costs a snprintf() call per number.

endchoice
